List every element whose board status is integrating and say which of four
things it is, with the evidence:

  awaiting_landing        accepted code whose candidate tree is NOT on the fresh
                          protected trunk: the landing act is still owed
  empty_delta_board_only  repository_delta=empty: the only landing act is a
                          board-state commit
  landed_on_trunk         the candidate tree is the tree of an ancestor of the
                          fresh protected ref that postdates the record's base —
                          the same proof close-landed applies, and nothing weaker
  deferred                the record carries the explicit deferral marker set by
                          defer_cr: a human parked it, and it is not backlog

Everything the view cannot establish — no Change Request record, a record that
cannot be read or contradicts itself, a git read that failed — is reported as
indeterminate and is never one of the four. A commit message that mentions an
element id is not evidence and is not consulted.

Each row carries candidate_tree_on_trunk (yes/no/indeterminate),
repository_delta, the deferral marker with its reason, and the age since the
revision was accepted. landing_backlog counts awaiting_landing plus
empty_delta_board_only; deferred, landed and indeterminate rows are excluded.

